# XingAI Foundation

Applies to every `xingai-*` repo and public `*.xingai.app` product app.

## Mobile-First

- Design for 320-430px usable width first.
- Touch targets should be at least 44x44 CSS px.
- Use safe-area padding for fixed top/bottom chrome.
- Default to single-column layouts on phones.
- Put primary decision content before decorative chrome in DOM order.
- Do not fake OS status bars in the DOM.

## Navigation Chrome

Every shipped product surface should expose the same nav destinations across form factors.

| Surface | Mobile | Desktop |
|---|---|---|
| Top bar | menu, brand/title, language, theme, profile/login if applicable | sticky top bar or reachable controls |
| Side menu | sheet/drawer with full nav + settings fallback | same sheet or persistent sidebar |
| Footer bar | fixed bottom tab bar for primary destinations | no bottom tab bar |
| Footer links | legal + help in drawer/page footer | same legal links in footer |

Rules:

1. Never hide language or theme on mobile unless the side drawer repeats them.
2. Long titles should truncate cleanly.
3. Main content needs bottom padding when bottom nav exists.
4. Mark unreleased nav items `Soon`; do not ship empty routes.
5. Do not expose internal labels like V1/V2 in user-facing nav or titles.

## Language

Required locales:

- `en`
- `zh`
- `ko`

All new user-facing strings should go through the repo i18n layer. Product AI prompts and outputs should respect selected language where applicable.

## Theme

- Support light and dark themes.
- Use repo theme convention: `next-themes`, `.dark`, or `data-theme`.
- Avoid theme flash.
- Update `theme-color` metadata where supported.
- Use repo tokens, preferably `oklch`; do not introduce random primary hex colors.

## Legal

Every public product must link:

- `/legal/privacy`
- `/legal/terms`
- `/legal/disclaimer`

AI lifestyle/travel/style/research products must say suggestions are informational and users should verify before action. Finance products need risk-first copy and no return promises.

## SEO + AEO

Before calling a product route shipped:

- `metadataBase`
- unique title + description per route
- canonical URL
- Open Graph + Twitter card
- sitemap.xml
- robots.txt
- correct `<html lang>`
- `llms.txt`
- short factual FAQ
- JSON-LD where applicable

## Pre-Ship Checklist

- [ ] Mobile layout verified at ~375px
- [ ] Top bar, side drawer, and bottom nav wired where applicable
- [ ] en / zh / ko strings complete
- [ ] Light/dark readable
- [ ] Privacy, Terms, Disclaimer linked
- [ ] SEO/AEO files updated
- [ ] No internal version labels in UI
